      "created": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z",
      "history": [
        {
          "action": "created via batch",
          "actor": "Tom",
          "actor_kind": "Unknown",
          "at": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.822425600Z",
          "reason": null
        }
      ],
      "id": "REQ-0105",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "The ack flag was ignored on the streaming path, so followed messages were redelivered as unread by a later plain read, contradicting documented --ack semantics.",
      "statement": "When a follow subscription is opened with ack enabled, the daemon shall advance the consumer cursor for each streamed message that is successfully delivered.",
      "status": "Draft",
      "tags": [
        "v0.2.2",
        "receive"
      ],
      "tests": [],
      "title": "read --follow --ack must advance the consumer cursor for streamed messages",
      "updated": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z"
    },
    "REQ-0106": {
      "acceptance": [
        "A daemon crash during read --follow yields a non-zero exit and an error message"
      ],
      "created": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z",
      "history": [
        {
          "action": "created via batch",
          "actor": "Tom",
          "actor_kind": "Unknown",
          "at": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.822472800Z",
          "reason": null
        }
      ],
      "id": "REQ-0106",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Folding every I/O error into a clean exit made a daemon crash indistinguishable from a normal stream end for monitoring scripts.",
      "statement": "The read --follow command shall exit zero only on a clean end-of-stream (EOF) and shall exit non-zero on any other I/O failure (connection reset, broken pipe, truncated frame).",
      "status": "Draft",
      "tags": [
        "v0.2.2",
        "receive"
      ],
      "tests": [],
      "title": "read --follow must surface a stream failure as a non-zero exit",
      "updated": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z"
    },
    "REQ-0107": {
      "acceptance": [
        "A subscriber that misses N messages in a burst receives a Lagged frame reporting N"
      ],
      "created": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z",
      "history": [
        {
          "action": "created via batch",
          "actor": "Tom",
          "actor_kind": "Unknown",
          "at": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.822521500Z",
          "reason": null
        }
      ],
      "id": "REQ-0107",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A hardcoded dropped:1 understated bursts and the compensating notice could itself be dropped, leaving a silent gap.",
      "statement": "When a follow subscriber falls behind, the daemon shall accumulate the true count of dropped messages per subscriber and deliver it in a single Lagged frame once the channel drains, rather than reporting a fixed count of one or dropping the notice.",
      "status": "Draft",
      "tags": [
        "v0.2.2",
        "receive"
      ],
      "tests": [],
      "title": "Streaming lag signal must be accurate and never silently lost",
      "updated": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z"
    },
    "REQ-0108": {
      "acceptance": [
        "A length prefix above the maximum returns an InvalidData error with no large allocation",
        "A normal frame round-trips"
      ],
      "created": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z",
      "history": [
        {
          "action": "created via batch",
          "actor": "Tom",
          "actor_kind": "Unknown",
          "at": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.822591300Z",
          "reason": null
        }
      ],
      "id": "REQ-0108",
      "kind": "Constraint",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "Trusting an attacker/bug-controlled 4-byte length allowed an unbounded allocation per local connection before any request parsing.",
      "statement": "The IPC frame reader shall reject a length prefix exceeding a fixed maximum (16 MiB) before allocating a buffer.",
      "status": "Draft",
      "tags": [
        "v0.2.2",
        "hardening"
      ],
      "tests": [],
      "title": "IPC frame reader must bound the length prefix before allocating",
      "updated": "2026-07-01T07:54:20.807428800Z"
    },
    "REQ-0109": {
